We define the notion of \emph{Kollár component} in two-steps:
\begin{itemize}
    \item[(1)] Let $x\in (X:=\operatorname{Spec} R,\Delta)$ be a klt singularity with a local ring $R$ essentially of finite type over $\mathbb{C}$. We say that a prime divisor $S$ over $x\in X$ is a \emph{Kollar component} if there exists a proper birational morphism $\pi:X'\to X$ such that
\begin{itemize}
    \item[(a)] $S$ is the unique exceptional divisor,
    \item[(b)] $-(K_{X'}+S+\pi^{-1}_*\Delta)$ is $\mathbb{Q}$-Cartier and ample over $X$, and 
    \item[(c)] $(X',S+\pi^{-1}_*\Delta)$ is plt.
\end{itemize}
The morphism $\pi:X'\to X$ is called the \emph{plt extraction} of the Kollár component $S$.
\item[(2)] Let $(X,\Delta)$ be a klt pair in general, and let $S$ be a prime divisor over $X$. We say that $S$ is a \emph{Kollár component} if
\begin{itemize}
    \item[(a)] $S\subseteq X$, or
    \item[(b)] there exists a (not necessarily closed) point $x\in X$ such that $S$ is a Kollár component of $(X_x,\Delta_x)$.
\end{itemize}
\end{itemize}

\label{Kollar}
Let $x\in X:=\operatorname{Spec} R$ be an $n$-dimensional klt germ over $\mathbb{C}$ of characteristic $0$, and let $S$ be a Kollár component over $x\in X$. For every $f\in R$ and every order $r$ differential operator $P:R\to R$,
\begin{equation} \label{ineq}
\mathrm{ord}_S(Pf)\ge \mathrm{ord}_S(f)-rA_X(S).
\end{equation}

